{
  "format": 1,
  "name": "residential_lifecycle",
  "spec": ["residential 4.1", "residential 4.2", "residential 2", "REH 4.2"],
  "description": "Init's call order on a new 8 x 8 city whose developers' population maps have tract size 2: services, developers, the demand node (tested), the message server with the two occupant subscriptions (0x99EF1142, 0x99EF1143), the budget simulator, the simulator, AddAgent at levels 0, 10, 6, 4 ('cSC4ResidentialSimulator', flags 2), the 20 history queue lengths (2 each; 0xCA545CAB + g and 0xCA545CCA + g interleaved for g = 0..8, then 0x4A8A3FE2, 0x4A8A3FE5), the ordinance-effect refresh, then the four departments (health 0x09188F42 / name 0xCA493A56 at 0.25, its secondary 0xAA538CB3 / 0xCA538D98 at 1.0, education 0x09188F4C / 0x6A493A66 at 0.25, its secondary 0x4A538CC6 / 0x8A538DAC at 1.0; max 120 x 0.01f). P = E = 2 (the R$ developer's map), proximity size 1; the iterator covers the 4 x 4 population tracts, fresh at (0, 0). A second Init takes no message server, subscribes nothing, does not refresh the ordinances and creates no department. Shutdown: RemoveAgent, the two unsubscriptions, the message server and budget, the four departments, Shutdown of the 25 grids in section 2 order, the services, then one Release per list entry (null entries skipped); a second Shutdown does nothing; Init afterwards subscribes again.",
